a rising number of educators deciding to  leave clark county school district 8  news now reporter kristen drummond  joining us live in the newsroom with the  issue and the concerns directly from  educators kristin well each board  meeting agenda  lists the teachers leaving documents  from the last three board meetings show  nearly 400 people deciding to  not continue with ccsd a significant  jump from the list posted in january and  february  now the reasons why vary but some  educators tell me  they're done just dissatisfied  dissatisfied  disgruntled and disappointed i have too  much experience and i have too much  education to be paid so low jeremy locke  says  low pay is one of the reasons he and his  wife plan to quit teaching in the clark  county school district next month  it's so political the duo came here one  year ago to continue building their  careers but  changed their mind about ccsd huge  problem of  valuing your people i see educators  making exit plans  national education association of  southern nevada president vicki kreidel  notices  this issue i personally know people who  just quit  and left because they don't feel  respected the clark county education  association sent me a statement  the teachers union president says the  numbers we're seeing so far  are slightly higher than last year  however they are lower than years prior  to last  it's hard to say for sure as we won't  know any final numbers until the end of  the school year  ccsd currently reports 479 current  teacher vacancies  that's around 2 percent of the roughly  18 thousand educators in positions  ccsd normally reports a teacher shortage  at the beginning of each school year  it remains unknown if it may double as  more educators decide to leave next  month  how's the morale for you and how was it  among your colleagues  the morale has been a struggle for  everyone this year ryan frommeltz does  not plan to leave his job despite his  concerns  while he stays the locks seek new  opportunities in education  outside nevada there's challenges to all  districts  the district created a commission last  year to focus on recruiting  and retaining educators reporting in the  newsroom kristen drummond  8 news now
 

